ce rule, are recorded in `auth_service.REGISTRATION_MESSAGES` for TestGenerator/CoverageToTestPlanner. Files materialized as skeletons only (signatures, routes, labeled form markup): `index.js` and `authApi.ts` are complete connectors; service/route/page internals and the current `HomePage`/router/shell wiring are left to TestDrivenDeveloper. Remaining work not materialized due to the 8-file DESIGN budget: SPA entry (`main.tsx` BrowserRouter + SessionProvider), the `/register` route, the home-page \"Sign in\" entry control, and the DB schema/seed bodies — all fully specified as interfaces below.\",\n  \"interfaces\": [\n    {\n      \"interface_id\": \"REQ-1-1-1-UI-REGISTER-PAGE\",\n      \"req_id\": \"REQ-1-1-1\",\n      \"type\": \"UI\",\n      \"name\": \"RegisterPage\",\n      \"file_path\": \"frontend/src/features/auth/RegisterPage.tsx\",\n      \"first_line\": 1,\n      \"responsibility\": \"Registration form reached only from the unique \\\"Create an account\\\" link on the sign-in page. Owns client-side rule checking, POST /api/auth/register, and itemized per-field error rendering while preserving username/email input.\",\n      \"specification\": \"Exports `RegisterPage({ onRegistered })` (default export too) and `submitRegistration(input): Promise<RegisterAccountResult>`. Required controls, exactly one each: textbox labeled `Username`, textbox labeled `Email`, password input labeled `Password`, password input labeled `Confirm password`, initially unchecked checkbox named `Agree to the terms`, enabled button named `Create account`. Passwords must never be rendered/echoed anywhere. On submit: run client rules (username /^[a-z0-9]+(?:-[a-z0-9]+)*$/ length 1-39; email trimmed, <=254 chars, exactly one '@', >=1 dot with non-empty labels; password 12-128 chars with upper+lower+digit+non-alphanumeric and no whitespace; confirmation identical to password; terms checked), then POST via `registerAccount`. Must report ALL invalid fields in one submission (no early return / no first-error-only) so the example (username '-bad', email 'not-an-email', password 'short', confirmation 'different', terms unchecked) shows Username format is invalid + Email format is invalid + Password requirements are not satisfied + Agree to terms is required together with 'different' producing the confirm-mismatch message; the submit button stays enabled/actionable after failure. On API 400, `fieldErrors` must map to the corresponding field and 'Username already exists' must appear beside Username while both attempted username and email values remain visible. On success: keep no password in state, call `onRegistered(input)`, and the shell navigates to the sign-in page (no email-verification page). No success is shown for a rejected submission.\",\n      \"inputs\": \"RegisterPageProps { onRegistered?: (input: RegisterAccountInput) => void }\",\n      \"outputs\": \"Rendered form + status text \",\n      \"callers\": [\n        \"frontend/src/App.tsx route /register\",\n        \"frontend/src/features/auth/SignInPage.tsx (via the Create an account link)\"\n      ],\n      \"callees\": [\n        \"frontend/src/api/authApi.ts:registerAccount\",\n        \"REQ-1-1-1-UI-SIGNIN-PAGE (navigation target on success)\"\n      ],\n      \"test_focus\": [\n        \"exactly one control per required label/role\",\n        \"all-invalid submission surfaces every field message at once and keeps username/email\",\n        \"duplicate username + fresh email -> 'Username already exists' retains both values\",\n        \"password value never present in DOM text\",\n        \"successful submit calls the API once and reaches the sign-in page\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"interface_id\": \"REQ-1-1-1-UI-SIGNIN-PAGE\",\n      \"req_id\": \"REQ-1-1-1\",\n      \"type\": \"UI\",\n      \"name\": \"SignInPage\",\n      \"file_path\": \"frontend/src/features/auth/SignInPage.tsx\",\n      \"first_line\": 1,\n      \"responsibility\": \"Account-access page and the sole source of the \\\"Create an account\\\" link to the registration page. Accepts username-or-email identifier plus password and updates global authenticated state on success.\",\n      \"specification\": \"Exports `SignInPage({ onSignedIn })` (default export too). Renders a `Sign in` heading, a text input labeled `Username or email`, a password input labeled `Password`, a `Sign in` button, and exactly one `Create an account` `Link` to `/register`. On submit it calls `signIn({ identifier, password })`; on success it calls `onSignedIn(account)` so the shell writes the account into the shared session context and enters the workspace; on failure it renders the returned error message. The just-registered account's email (`<name>@example.test`) must be accepted as the identifier immediately after registration.\",\n      \"inputs\": \"SignInPageProps { onSignedIn?: (account: AuthAccount) => void }\",\n      \"outputs\": \"Rendered account-access page\",\n      \"callers\": [\n        \"frontend/src/App.tsx route /signin\",\n        \"frontend/src/pages/HomePage.tsx Sign in entry\"\n      ],\n      \"callees\": [\n        \"frontend/src/api/authApi.ts:signIn\",\n        \"REQ-1-1-1-UI-REGISTER-PAGE (Create an account link)\"\n      ],\n      \"test_focus\": [\n        \"Create an account link target is the registration route\",\n        \"successful sign-in updates global session (not local state)\",\n        \"registered email identifier signs in successfully\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"interface_id\": \"REQ-1-1-1-UI-SESSION-PROVIDER\",\n      \"req_id\": \"REQ-1-1-1\",\n      \"type\": \"UI\",\n      \"name\": \"SessionProvider / useAuthSession\",\n      \"file_path\": \"frontend/src/features/auth/SessionProvider.tsx\",\n      \"first_line\": 1,\n      \"responsibility\": \"Single global source of truth for authentication state so registration/sign-in outcomes and reload-safe current-user display are not page-local.\",\n      \"specification\": \"Exports `AuthSessionContext`, `SessionProvider({ children })` and `useAuthSession()`. Value shape: `{ account: AuthAccount | null, status: 'loading' | 'ready', setAccount(account|null), refresh(): Promise<void>, signOut(): Promise<void> }`. On mount it must restore the durable session via GET /api/auth/session (so the signed-in username is visible after a full reload) and expose `setAccount` for the registration/sign-in flows. `signOut` clears the cookie and global state. `useAuthSession` must throw a descriptive error when used outside the provider. The app shell/header, protected/public routing and current-user display must all consume this context rather than duplicating user state. TestDrivenDeveloper implements the runtime behavior.\",\n      \"inputs\": \"{ children: ReactNode }\",\n      \"outputs\": \"AuthSessionValue context\",\n      \"callers\": [\n        \"frontend/src/main.tsx (SPA entry with BrowserRouter)\",\n        \"frontend/src/App.tsx shell\"\n      ],\n      \"callees\": [\n        \"frontend/src/api/authApi.ts:fetchSession\",\n        \"frontend/src/api/authApi.ts:logout\"\n      ],\n      \"test_focus\": [\n        \"unauthenticated chrome before the action, authenticated current username after\",\n        \"account survives reload via session restore\",\n        \"setAccount from registration/sign-in updates every consumer\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"interface_id\": \"REQ-1-1-1-API-FRONTEND-AUTH-CLIENT\",\n      \"req_id\": \"REQ-1-1-1\",\n      \"type\": \"API\",\n      \"name\": \"authApi client\",\n      \"file_path\": \"frontend/src/api/authApi.ts\",\n      \"first_line\": 1,\n      \"responsibility\": \"Typed HTTP client for the account-access endpoints; normalizes per-field registration errors for the page.\",\n      \"specification\": \"Exports types `AuthAccount { id, username, email, emailVerified }`, `RegisterFieldErrors` (keys username|email|password|confirmPassword|agreeToTerms), `RegisterAccountInput`, `RegisterAccountResult`, `SignInInput`, `SignInResult`, and functions `registerAccount(input)` -> POST /api/auth/register (201 `{account}` -> `{ok:true,account}`; 400 `{fieldErrors}` -> `{ok:false,fieldErrors}`), `signIn({identifier,password})` -> POST /api/auth/login, `fetchSession()` -> GET /api/auth/session returning `account|null`, `logout()` -> POST /api/auth/logout. Must use the shared `apiClient` from `frontend/src/api/index.ts` (withCredentials) so the session cookie is sent and interceptor-normalized errors are surfaced.\",\n      \"inputs\": \"RegisterAccountInput, SignInInput\",\n      \"outputs\": \"RegisterAccountResult, SignInResult, AuthAccount|null, void\",\n      \"callers\": [\n        \"frontend/src/features/auth/RegisterPage.tsx\",\n        \"frontend/src/features/auth/SignInPage.tsx\",\n        \"frontend/src/features/auth/SessionProvider.tsx\"\n      ],\n      \"callees\": [\n        \"frontend/src/api/index.ts (axios instance + error interceptor)\"\n      ],\n      \"test_focus\": [\n        \"registers via POST /api/auth/register and surfaces fieldErrors on 400\",\n        \"sends credentials/cookies for session restore\",\n        \"never exposes the password in its returned payloads\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"interface_id\": \"REQ-1-1-1-API-AUTH-ROUTES\",\n      \"req_id\": \"REQ-1-1-1\",\n      \"type\": \"API\",\n      \"name\": \"authRoutes (Express HTTP boundary)\",\n      \"file_path\": \"backend/src/routes/auth_routes.js\",\n      \"first_line\": 1,\n      \"responsibility\": \"Express router exposing registration, sign-in, session restore, and sign-out under /api/auth, plus the shared HttpOnly session cookie contract.\",\n      \"specification\": \"Exports `createAuthRouter(): Router` and `SESSION_COOKIE='session_token'`. POST /register -> 201 `{account:{id,username,email,emailVerified:true}}` on success, 400 `{fieldErrors:{username?,email?,password?,confirmPassword?,agreeToTerms?}}` on validation/conflict failure (never echoes the password). POST /login with `{identifier,password}` -> 200 `{account}` and Set-Cookie `session_token=<token>; Path=/; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax; Max-Age=<SESSION_MAX_AGE_SECONDS>` or 401 `{error}`. GET /session -> 200 `{account: Account|null}` read from the cookie, enabling reload-safe restore. POST /logout -> 200 `{ok:true}` and `Max-Age=0` cookie clear. Router stays thin: all rules, hashing and persistence delegate to auth_service. Mounted at `/api/auth` in backend/src/index.js.\",\n      \"inputs\": \"Express Request (json body, Cookie header)\",\n      \"outputs\": \"JSON responses + Set-Cookie headers\",\n      \"callers\": [\n        \"backend/src/index.js (app.use('/api/auth', createAuthRouter()))\"\n      ],\n      \"callees\": [\n        \"backend/src/services/auth_service.js:registerAccount\",\n        \"backend/src/services/auth_service.js:signIn\",\n        \"backend/src/services/auth_service.js:getSessionAccount\",\n        \"backend/src/services/auth_service.js:signOut\"\n      ],\n      \"test_focus\": [\n        \"supertest: 201 verified account on valid registration, 400 fieldErrors map otherwise\",\n        \"login sets the session cookie; session endpoint returns the account; logout clears it\",\n        \"unknown /api/* paths return JSON 404 rather than the SPA shell\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"interface_id\": \"REQ-1-1-1-FUNC-AUTH-SERVICE\",\n      \"req_id\": \"REQ-1-1-1\",\n      \"type\": \"FUNC\",\n      \"name\": \"authService\",\n      \"file_path\": \"backend/src/services/auth_service.js\",\n      \"first_line\": 1,\n      \"responsibility\": \"Owns registration rules and messages, credential verification, password hashing, and durable session lifecycle against the shared database scaffold.\",\n      \"specification\": \"Exports constants USERNAME_PATTERN=/^[a-z0-9]+(?:-[a-z0-9]+)*$/, USERNAME_MAX_LENGTH=39, EMAIL_MAX_LENGTH=254, PASSWORD_MIN_LENGTH=12, PASSWORD_MAX_LENGTH=128, SESSION_MAX_AGE_SECONDS, and the message maps REGISTRATION_MESSAGES (usernameExists:'Username already exists', usernameFormat:'Username format is invalid', emailFormat:'Email format is invalid', emailExists, passwordPolicy:'Password requirements are not satisfied', confirmMismatch, termsRequired:'Agree to terms is required') and SIGN_IN_MESSAGES. Functions: `validateRegistrationInput(input)` returning a field-error map that reports EVERY invalid field simultaneously (message content must contain the required substrings); `registerAccount(input)` -> `{ok:true,account:{id,username,email,emailVerified:true}}` or `{ok:false,fieldErrors}`, storing a sign-in-capable account with verified email, rejecting duplicate username/email by case-insensitive comparison of the trimmed values, and never persisting or returning plaintext passwords (one-way salted hash via `hashPassword`); `signIn({identifier,password})` -> `{ok:true,account,token}` or `{ok:false,message}` matching lower-cased username OR trimmed lower-cased email; `getSessionAccount(token)` and `signOut(token)` for the durable sessions table; `findAccountByIdentifier(identifier)`. All persistence goes through the shared scaffold (`../database`: run/get/withTransaction, accounts/sessions tables).\",\n      \"inputs\": \"RegisterAccountInput, {identifier,password}, session token string\",\n      \"outputs\": \"Field-error maps, account projections, session tokens\",\n      \"callers\": [\n        \"backend/src/routes/auth_routes.js\"\n      ],\n      \"callees\": [\n        \"backend/src/database/init_db.js (schema)\",\n        \"backend/src/database/db_runtime.js (run/get/withTransaction)\",\n        \"backend/src/database/seed_db.js (seeded account lookup path)\"\n      ],\n      \"test_focus\": [\n        \"all-invalid payload returns all four messages together in one call\",\n        \"duplicate username case-insensitively rejected, unused email accepted\",\n        \"password policy enforced per rule (length, upper, lower, digit, special, no whitespace)\",\n        \"successful registration is immediately sign-in-able and email marked verified\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"interface_id\": \"REQ-1-1-1-DB-RUNTIME-ENTRYPOINT\",\n      \"req_id\": \"REQ-1-1-1\",\n      \"type\": \"DB\",\n      \"name\": \"backend runtime entrypoint (app + startup init/seed)\",\n      \"file_path\": \"backend/src/index.js\",\n      \"first_line\": 1,\n      \"responsibility\": \"Hosts the built frontend dist and the API on the single port 3411, and guarantees the database schema plus deterministic seed data exist before serving requests.\",\n      \"specification\": \"Exports `createApp()` (cors, express.json, `/api/auth` router, JSON 404 for unknown /api paths, static `frontend/dist`, SPA catch-all to index.html) and `start()` which awaits `initializeDatabase()` then `seedDatabase()` before `app.listen(PORT)` with PORT default 3411. `require.main === module` triggers start(). This is the contract that makes account registration durable across reloads and makes the authored frontend the user-facing app.\",\n      \"inputs\": \"process.env.PORT | ARC_WEB_PORT\",\n      \"outputs\": \"Listening Express server on port 3411\",\n      \"callers\": [\n        \"npm run start (node src/index.js)\",\n        \"backend/tests/* integration suites via createApp()\"\n      ],\n      \"callees\": [\n        \"backend/src/routes/auth_routes.js:createAuthRouter\",\n        \"backend/src/database/init_db.js:initializeDatabase\",\n        \"backend/src/database/seed_db.js:seedDatabase\"\n      ],\n      \"test_focus\": [\n        \"server boots on 3411 and serves the SPA shell\",\n        \"/api/auth/* reachable from the hosted origin\",\n        \"startup performs schema init + idempotent seed\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"interface_id\": \"REQ-1-1-1-DB-ACCOUNTS-SEED\",\n      \"req_id\": \"REQ-1-1-1\",\n      \"type\": \"DB\",\n      \"name\": \"accounts + sessions schema and deterministic seed\",\n      \"file_path\": \"backend/src/database/seed_db.js\",\n      \"first_line\": 1,\n      \"responsibility\": \"Owns the persistent account/session tables and the deterministic, idempotent application seed data required by the scenarios.\",\n      \"specification\": \"Extends the existing scaffold rather than adding a parallel store. `init_db.js` (idempotent CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS) must define `accounts(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, username TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE, email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE, password_hash TEXT NOT NULL, email_verified INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0, created_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)` and `sessions(token TEXT PRIMARY KEY, account_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES accounts(id) ON DELETE CASCADE, created_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, expires_at TEXT NOT NULL)`. `seed_db.js` must idempotently upsert (INSERT OR IGNORE / upsert by unique key) the pre-existing GIVEN account `alice-dev` / `alice.dev@example.test` / password `Valid-password-123!` with `email_verified = 1`, using the same one-way hash helper as the service, so the seeded account is sign-in-able through the normal path. Seeding runs on application startup (via `start()`), via `npm run db:seed`, and through `createTestDatabaseHarness()`/`seedDefault()` for isolated test databases; it must be safe to run repeatedly and must not introduce feature-specific hidden fixtures or fabricated rows beyond the account declared by the requirement.\",\n      \"inputs\": \"none (idempotent bootstrap), harness dbPath for tests\",\n      \"outputs\": \"Seeded accounts/sessions tables\",\n      \"callers\": [\n        \"backend/src/index.js:start\",\n        \"backend/src/database/test_harness.js:createRuntimeFacade.seedDefault\",\n        \"npm run db:seed\"\n      ],\n      \"callees\": [\n        \"backend/src/database/init_db.js:initializeDatabase\",\n        \"backend/src/database/db_runtime.js:withTransaction\"\n      ],\n      \"test_focus\": [\n        \"repeated seeding keeps exactly one `alice-dev` row\",\n        \"seeded account signs in with `Valid-password-123!`\",\n    