[2026-09-26T17:24:51.135+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-2]   "summary": "REQ-1-1-2 is a leaf node (no children, no visual references) that owns the executable sign-in slice: credential verification, generic failure semantics, durable session creation/restore, global authenticated UI state, and protected navigation. Existing code from the dependency REQ-1-1-1 already provided the account-access page, the shared SessionProvider, the auth API client, the auth route/service, and the sqlite `accounts`/`sessions` scaffold; no interface records existed for the dependency, so this node mints its own stable ids while reusing those files as the baseline (SignInPage, SessionProvider, authApi, auth_routes, auth_service, init_db, seed_db). New owned boundaries materialized as small skeletons: shared account chrome `AccountMenu.tsx` (upper-right account menu reading global session), `ProtectedRoute.tsx` (reload-safe authorization gate), `backend/src/services/session_context.js` (single backend 'current user for this request' resolver built on getSessionAccount, failing closed with 401), and `features/workspace/WorkspacePage.tsx` (thin post-sign-in destination that renders session state and explicit empty states instead of invented organization/repository/work-item records). App.tsx was rewired so a successful sign-in updates the shared session and navigates to the protected /workspace route, and the generic failure text was aligned to the required exact string 'Invalid credentials' in the service constant and the form default so unknown identifier, wrong password, and unavailable account are indistinguishable. Persistence contracts stay in the existing scaffold: the alice-dev / alice.dev@example.test / Valid-password-123! GIVEN record is seeded idempotently in seed_db.js (normal startup path via backend/src/index.js -> initializeDatabase + seedDatabase), and the sessions contract is specified as token + account_id + active status with refresh-safe expiry; the DB interface records the required idempotent schema evolution (session `active`, account availability) that the TDD stage must implement. No business logic, validation, or seeding logic was implemented in DESIGN beyond connector wiring.",
