[2026-09-26T17:24:51.278+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-2]       "specification": "Reads `{ account, status }` from useAuthSession(). While status === 'loading' it renders a loading placeholder (data-testid 'session-loading') so a valid cookie session is not mistaken for unauthenticated during restore. When status === 'ready' and account is null it renders <Navigate replace to='/login' state={{ from: location.pathname }} />. Otherwise it renders the children. Consuming the shared context (not a local flag) is what makes the previously accessible protected page still show the signed-in user after refresh/reopen, while a failed sign-in still requires authentication.",
